## Continuous Narrative for Demo

> *"When a user uploads a PDF, the system extracts the text, classifies it as either a Safety Data Sheet or Technical Data Sheet using Azure OpenAI, chunks it using token-based splitting with overlap, generates 3072-dimensional embeddings, and indexes everything to Azure AI Search — all in real-time.*
>
> *When the user asks a question, it first goes to our Query Classifier agent which determines whether they're asking about safety information (SDS) or technical specifications (TDS). This doc_type is critical — it filters all subsequent searches to the right document category.*
>
> *The question then enters the Reasoning Agent, which has access to the retrieve_chunks tool. The agent decides whether it needs to fetch document evidence. If it does, the tool embeds the query, searches the vector index, and returns relevant chunks. This agent-tool loop can iterate up to 5 times for complex questions.*
>
> *Finally, the agent generates a grounded answer citing the exact source document and section — no hallucinations, just facts pulled from your uploaded chemistry documents."*

---

This flow demonstrates a **fully serverless, enterprise-grade RAG system** that combines agentic reasoning with vector search to deliver accurate, source-grounded answers over chemistry documents.
